Package: [[name]]
# Not [[version]]: that is the raw Maven version, and apt compares on this line. This is the
# agent module's version with -SNAPSHOT rewritten to ~snapshot.<run>, which sorts below the release
# rather than above it.
Version: [[agent.package.version]]
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: fuin.org <info@fuin.org>
Homepage: https://github.com/porelo-ai/porelo
# The native binary links against both; jdeb does not read it to find out. NativeLinkageCheck
# holds these floors to the binary.
Depends: porelo (>= [[porelo.minimum.version]]), libc6 (>= [[package.glibc.floor]]), zlib1g (>= 1:[[package.zlib.floor]])
# What the setup script and Tasks1.Installable() list: every package providing it is an agent a
# person can choose. The name is Porelo's.
Provides: porelo-agent
Description: [[description]] [[agent.cli.version]]
 Installs into /usr/libexec/porelo/agents, where the porelo binary looks for
 agents. Nothing needs to be registered: porelo scans that directory and asks
 whatever it finds to describe itself, so installing this package is enough.
 .
 Antigravity CLI is https://github.com/google-antigravity/antigravity-cli,
 invoked as "agy". Its image installs the CLI from a verified pinned archive.
 .
 The package version is this agent's own version, independent of Porelo's release
 line. The agent CLI version it installs is on the Description line above, so
 "dpkg -s porelo-agent-agy" answers which Antigravity CLI this package fetches,
 without consulting the definition.
